      "description": "Watch Paris Saint Germain vs Slovan Bratislava highlights and goals from UEFA Champions League on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 9, 2026. The UEFA Champions League atmosphere was electric on September 9, 2026, as a highly anticipated encounter unfolded with both teams seeking to make a statement. Fans witnessed a tactical battle where momentum shifted unexpectedly across two distinct halves of football. Clinical Start for Rennes Rennes began the match with intent, showcasing clinical finishing to stun the visitors. The breakthrough came early in the 9th minute when Sebastian Szymanski unleashed a precise left-footed strike from outside the box into the top left corner, finishing a rapid counter-attack orchestrated by Adrien Thomasson . Paris Saint-Germain struggled to find their rhythm early on, despite Ousmane Dembélé and Warren Zaïre-Emery attempting to pierce the home side's organized defense. As the first half progressed, PSG ramped up the pressure with a series of corners, but it was Rennes who struck again. In the 38th minute, Estéban Lepaul doubled the lead, slotting a right-footed shot into the bottom right corner following a well-placed cross from Przemyslaw Frankowski . The hosts headed into the break with a commanding 2-0 lead, leaving the Parisian giants with a mountain to climb. The Turning Point Seeking a spark, PSG introduced Ferran Torres and Mika Godts at the start of the second half. The tactical shift became even more evident when Fabián Ruiz entered the fray in the 60th minute. The substitution immediately paid dividends as PSG began to dominate possession and territory, forcing Brice Samba into several high-quality saves to deny Désiré Doué and Zaïre-Emery . The comeback gained traction in the 71st minute. Ferran Torres found the back of the net with a clinical finish from the center of the box, assisted by Fabián Ruiz . After a brief VAR review, the goal was confirmed, slashing the deficit and setting up a grandstand finish. Late Drama and Parity With momentum firmly on their side, the visitors pushed for an equalizer. It arrived in the 82nd minute when Fabián Ruiz turned provider once again, delivering a cross that Ferran Torres met with a powerful header into the bottom corner. The closing stages were frantic, with Ludovic Blas nearly reclaiming the lead for Rennes and Mika Godts missing a golden opportunity for PSG in stoppage time. Ultimately, the points were shared in a contest that highlighted both Rennes ' early brilliance and Paris Saint-Germain 's relentless spirit."
